From 66ae252d48a52e385155f7c5ee44346c226003d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D. Zack Garza" <dzackgarza@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:30:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] fix: let a missing libbliss-cxx fall through under
 -Dbliss=enabled

The pkg-config probes in the bliss lookup were required: get_option('bliss'),
so with -Dbliss=enabled -- or auto_features=enabled, which turns feature options
into enabled -- a missing libbliss-cxx aborted the configure before the
pkg-config fallback or the raw library was tried. disabler: true does not make a
required dependency optional; it only disables targets that depend on an
unfound one.

Both pkg-config probes are now required: false, the whole chain is skipped when
the feature is disabled, and only the final cc.find_library carries
required: bliss_opt. So: disabled probes nothing and leaves bliss disabled;
auto finds whichever of the three exists and otherwise disables it without
failing; enabled accepts a pkg-config name or the raw library and fails only
when neither exists -- from the last probe, as before.

The comment now states the assumption the raw fallback makes: a library found
only by name is assumed to be built with the headers' default big-number
representation, which is what Sage's own USE_GMP=OFF spkg installs. A
distribution library reached only through that path is the ABI mismatch this
code exists to avoid.

Resolution cases, run in the image against the extracted block with a feature
option: enabled + libbliss-cxx -> found; enabled with no pkg-config files ->
found through cc.find_library, no abort (the defect); auto with and without
pkg-config -> found; names that resolve nowhere -> auto and disabled return
"not found" with exit 0, while enabled fails with "C++ shared or static library
'...' not found" from the last probe; disabled with the library present ->
"not found", exit 0, no probe run.
---
 src/sage/graphs/meson.build | 38 +++++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/sage/graphs/meson.build b/src/sage/graphs/meson.build
index 971785b..b512129 100644
--- a/src/sage/graphs/meson.build
+++ b/src/sage/graphs/meson.build
@@ -1,17 +1,27 @@
-# Some distributions (Debian, Ubuntu) build libbliss with BLISS_USE_GMP,
-# which changes the layout of bliss::Stats.  Such a library records the
-# definition its consumers need in a pkg-config file named libbliss-cxx; the
-# name is bliss on other distributions.  Linking -lbliss alone leaves
-# bliss/bignum.hh on its default representation, so the Stats that bliss.pyx
-# hands to the library is smaller than the one the library writes and
-# canonical_form() corrupts the heap.  Sage's own bliss spkg builds with
-# USE_GMP=OFF and installs no pkg-config file, so it keeps using -lbliss.
-bliss = dependency('libbliss-cxx', required: get_option('bliss'), disabler: true)
-if not bliss.found()
-  bliss = dependency('bliss', required: get_option('bliss'), disabler: true)
-endif
-if not bliss.found()
-  bliss = cc.find_library('bliss', required: get_option('bliss'), disabler: true)
+# Some distributions (Debian, Ubuntu) build libbliss with BLISS_USE_GMP, which
+# changes the layout of bliss::Stats.  Such a library records the definition its
+# consumers need in a pkg-config file named libbliss-cxx; the name is bliss on
+# other distributions.  Linking -lbliss alone leaves bliss/bignum.hh on its
+# default representation, so the Stats that bliss.pyx hands to the library is
+# smaller than the one the library writes and canonical_form() corrupts the
+# heap.
+#
+# Only the last probe can satisfy 'enabled': a missing pkg-config name falls
+# through to the raw library, and a missing raw library fails the configure.
+# The raw library is assumed to be built with the headers' default
+# representation -- Sage's own bliss spkg builds with USE_GMP=OFF and installs
+# no pkg-config file -- so a distribution library found only this way would be
+# the ABI mismatch this code exists to avoid.
+bliss_opt = get_option('bliss')
+bliss = disabler()
+if not bliss_opt.disabled()
+  bliss = dependency('libbliss-cxx', required: false, disabler: true)
+  if not bliss.found()
+    bliss = dependency('bliss', required: false, disabler: true)
+  endif
+  if not bliss.found()
+    bliss = cc.find_library('bliss', required: bliss_opt, disabler: true)
+  endif
 endif
 
 mcqd = disabler()
